known_false_positives.description:
`ValueOrDefault` is templated on the default literal type. Using `0/100/50` makes `T=int`, so any JS number that is not an integer may get truncated during `ConvertFromV8`. Since these Cocoa properties are `double` (`minValue/maxValue/doubleValue`), prefer double defaults to preserve precision and avoid unintended narrowing.

```suggestion
  item.slider.minValue = settings.ValueOrDefault("minValue", 0.0);
  item.slider.maxValue = settings.ValueOrDefault("maxValue", 100.0);
  item.slider.doubleValue = settings.ValueOrDefault("value", 50.0);
```
